    <!-- 1. Introduction -->
    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    
    <h3>1.1 Purpose</h3>
    <p>
      The purpose of this Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document is to provide a complete, rigorous, and unambiguous technical specification for <strong>CareConnect360</strong>, a cloud-enabled, full-stack telemedicine and clinical management platform. This specification conforms to the <strong>IEEE Std 830-1998</strong> standard and establishes binding functional, performance, security, and interface baselines for academic lab evaluations, faculty reviews, and production deployment.
    </p>

    <h3>1.2 Scope of the System</h3>
    <p>
      Healthcare accessibility is frequently hindered by geographic isolation, long outpatient waiting queues, fragmented paper records, and accidental adverse drug interactions. <strong>CareConnect360</strong> resolves these bottlenecks through a browser-native clinical consultation hub:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dynamic Doctor-Patient Matchmaking:</strong> Multi-criteria search by medical specialty (Cardiology, Dermatology, Pediatrics, General Medicine), consultation fee, and real-time slot reservation without double-booking.</li>
      <li><strong>Native WebRTC Audio/Video Teleconsultation:</strong> Zero-install, peer-to-peer (P2P) HD audio/video consultation with microphone mute/unmute, camera toggle, screen sharing, PIP feed swapping, and dynamic watermark sync.</li>
      <li><strong>Clinical Decision Support System (CDSS):</strong> Real-time drug contraindication radar cross-checking prescribed medications against patient known allergies (e.g. Penicillin, NSAIDs).</li>
      <li><strong>Digitally Signed e-Prescriptions:</strong> Client-side cryptographic signature rendering and instant verifiable PDF downloads via jsPDF with QR verification codes.</li>
      <li><strong>Electronic Health Records (EHR) Vault:</strong> Centralized timeline logging patient vitals telemetry (BP, SpO2, Heart Rate) and diagnostic lab reports (.pdf, .png, .jpg).</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>1.3 Definitions, Acronyms, and Abbreviations</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Term / Acronym</th>
          <th>Definition &amp; Technical Context</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>SRS</strong></td>
          <td>Software Requirements Specification (IEEE Std 830-1998 recommended standard format).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>WebRTC</strong></td>
          <td>Web Real-Time Communication (W3C standard for browser-to-browser P2P audio/video streaming).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>PeerJS / STUN</strong></td>
          <td>Signaling layer and Session Traversal Utilities for NAT traversal and candidate discovery.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>CDSS</strong></td>
          <td>Clinical Decision Support System for algorithmic medication safety and allergy verification.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>JWT / RBAC</strong></td>
          <td>JSON Web Token for stateless authorization; Role-Based Access Control (Patient, Doctor, Admin).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>DTLS-SRTP</strong></td>
          <td>Datagram Transport Layer Security &amp; Secure Real-Time Transport Protocol (256-bit AES media encryption).</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 2. Overall Description -->
    <h2>2. Overall Description</h2>
    
    <h3>2.1 Product Perspective</h3>
    <p>
      CareConnect360 operates as an autonomous, multi-tier web application built upon modern decoupled architecture, combining an HTML5/CSS3/ES6 presentation tier, a Node.js/Express.js application tier, a `/peerjs` WebRTC signaling engine, and cloud/local persistence.
    </p>

    <div class="diagram-box">
      <div class="mermaid">
flowchart TD
    Client["Client Presentation Tier\n(HTML5 / CSS3 / ES6 / WebRTC)"]
    API["Application & Signaling Tier\n(Node.js / Express.js / PeerJS Engine)"]
    DB[("Data Persistence & Storage\n(Firestore / REST API / LocalStorage)")]
    STUN["Google STUN Infrastructure\n(stun.l.google.com:19302)"]

    Client <-->|RESTful JSON Endpoints| API
    Client <-->|WebRTC Signaling| API
    Client <===>|Direct P2P Encrypted Audio/Video Feed| Client
    Client -.->|NAT Traversal & Candidate Discovery| STUN
    API <-->|CRUD & Authentication| DB
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-caption">Figure 2.1: Multi-Tier Architectural Topology of CareConnect360</div>
    </div>

    <h3>2.2 User Roles &amp; Characteristics</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 22%;">User Persona</th>
          <th style="width: 20%;">Technical Skill</th>
          <th>Core Privileges &amp; Responsibilities</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Patient</strong></td>
          <td>Novice to Intermediate</td>
          <td>Register, browse verified specialist directory, book consultation appointments, join encrypted video room, upload lab reports, view vital trends, and download signed e-Prescriptions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Doctor / Specialist</strong></td>
          <td>Intermediate</td>
          <td>Manage OPD schedule, review patient intake vitals &amp; diagnostic history, conduct P2P video consultation, author prescriptions with CDSS contraindication alerts, and digitally sign prescriptions.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Administrator</strong></td>
          <td>High (DevOps)</td>
          <td>Monitor system uptime, manage doctor verification credentials, view platform audit logs, enforce data privacy compliance, and moderate user accounts.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- 3. System Features & Functional Requirements -->
    <h2>3. System Features &amp; Functional Requirements</h2>

    <h3>3.1 Module 1: Patient Intake, Discovery &amp; Scheduling</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Req ID</th>
          <th style="width: 30%;">Feature Description</th>
          <th>Input Validation &amp; Behavior</th>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Priority</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-1.1</strong></td>
          <td>Doctor Directory &amp; Filter</td>
          <td>Filters specialists by department, consultation fee, and real-time slot availability.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-1.2</strong></td>
          <td>Conflict-Free Slot Booking</td>
          <td>Real-time reservation preventing double-booking of any doctor in identical time slots.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-1.3</strong></td>
          <td>Clinical Intake Triage</td>
          <td>Captures chief complaint, symptom duration, allergy disclosures, and emergency waiver.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-med">Medium</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>3.2 Module 2: Low-Latency WebRTC P2P Teleconsultation</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Req ID</th>
          <th style="width: 30%;">Feature Description</th>
          <th>Input Validation &amp; Behavior</th>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Priority</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-2.1</strong></td>
          <td>P2P Video Session Handshake</td>
          <td>Connects to `/peerjs` signaling server, generates room peer IDs, and exchanges SDP offer/answer.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-2.2</strong></td>
          <td>Audio/Video Track Controls</td>
          <td>Enables live mute/unmute of microphone and camera on/off with instant UI indicator updates.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-2.3</strong></td>
          <td>Feed Swapping &amp; Screen Share</td>
          <td>Swaps local PIP preview with stage; dispatches screen share video stream via `getDisplayMedia()`.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-2.4</strong></td>
          <td>Dynamic Booked Doctor Watermark</td>
          <td>Queries active appointment ID and updates consultation top bar, watermark, and letterhead to match booked doctor.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>3.3 Module 3: CDSS Drug Radar &amp; Verifiable e-Prescription Pad</h3>
    <table class="content-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Req ID</th>
          <th style="width: 30%;">Feature Description</th>
          <th>Input Validation &amp; Behavior</th>
          <th style="width: 14%;">Priority</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-3.1</strong></td>
          <td>Allergy Contraindication Radar</td>
          <td>Scans prescribed active compounds against patient allergies (e.g. Penicillin) and triggers visual alerts.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-3.2</strong></td>
          <td>Digital Signature Rendering</td>
          <td>Binds doctor registration number, hospital credentials, and digital signature canvas to prescription record.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>FR-3.3</strong></td>
          <td>Verifiable PDF Compilation</td>
          <td>Instantly compiles and downloads signed PDF prescription with QR verification code using jsPDF.</td>
          <td><span class="priority-high">High</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

